# What this plugin needs from outside Hammerspoon.
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason. See Olm's lib/deps.lua.
# All three required, since this plugin is nothing but a thin front end onto them, with no
# partial service to offer if any is gone. defaults reads and writes the stored preference,
# both the hiding boolean and the show delay. osascript is what an empirical check on
# 2026-08-09 found actually makes the running Dock notice a hiding change right away, see
# this plugin's own CLAUDE.md for the finding. killall is what makes the running Dock notice
# a delay change instead, since System Events has no delay property to push through, an
# empirical check the same date also found, see the same CLAUDE.md. None of the three is a
# real risk on any machine this runs on, all three ship with every macOS, so required here
# documents the contract rather than guarding against a practical absence.
defaults  | system | /usr/bin/defaults  | required | reading and writing the Dock's auto hide preference and its show delay
osascript | system | /usr/bin/osascript | required | telling the running Dock to notice a hiding change immediately
killall   | system | /usr/bin/killall   | required | restarting the Dock so it notices a show delay change
